# SCM syntax highlighting & preventing 3-way merges
pixi.lock merge=binary linguist-language=YAML linguist-generated=true -diff
# Force LF on checkout everywhere. GitHub's windows-latest runners ship
# Git with core.autocrlf=true, which turned every vendored text file into
# CRLF — zigbuild/config/win-x86_64-full/subst.txt in particular, whose
# S-table parser then kept the trailing `"\r` on each value, producing a
# link arg like `-lmsimg32"\r` that zig's mingw import-lib existence check
# could not even stat (Win32 ERROR_INVALID_NAME -> zig error.Unexpected,
# "failed to check zig installation for DLL import libs"). Self-hosted
# kappa also has autocrlf=true yet never hit it — its checkout is gone,
# so that difference stays unexplained (a locally-written LF subst.txt is
# the likely reason). build.zig's parser now tolerates CRLF as well; this
# keeps the checkout itself sane.
* text=auto eol=lf
# R's source patches: patch -p1 applies them with no fuzz to LF sources,
# so they must be LF too. Explicit rather than auto: a CRLF-saved patch is
# normalized on commit, and the rule holds if the one above ever changes.
zigbuild/patches/** text eol=lf
